<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- MeshLLM installs versioned native runtimes outside the app bundle. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <!--
      Passkeys (src/passkey_ceremony.rs): Apple's passkey APIs require the app
      to be entitled for the credential's relying-party domain.

      *** RELEASE SETUP REQUIRED ***
      The plist is static, so the domain cannot be parameterized at build
      time: REPLACE `passkey-rp-id-unset.invalid` with the real webcredentials
      domain BEFORE signing, and make sure BOTH of these match exactly:
        1. this entitlement value (webcredentials:<domain>)
        2. BUZZ_PASSKEY_RP_ID=<domain> at runtime
      The placeholder is an RFC 2606 `.invalid` domain on purpose — with it
      still in place every passkey ceremony fails loudly at the platform
      boundary (and `require_real_rp_id` refuses it before any request) instead
      of minting a credential bound to the wrong RP.

      STEP 0 of the activation runbook (the ordered checklist lives in
      src/commands/passkey.rs):
        bash scripts/passkey-activation-check.sh
      It fails on this placeholder with the exact substitution, and then
      verifies the whole chain: BUZZ_PASSKEY_RP_ID, the AASA actually served at
      /.well-known/apple-app-site-association (the relay builds it from
      BUZZ_PASSKEY_TEAM_ID + this app's identifier), and this entitlement.
      A plist carries no comments Apple reads, so the domain truth lives in
      this comment plus that script — keep them in sync when substituting.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
    <array>
        <string>webcredentials:passkey-rp-id-unset.invalid</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
